==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Valiant D'arktanyan''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
First of all, always use D'arktanyan's Evolved Form, since it has higher general stats.

With that out of the way, Valiant D'arktanyan deals massive damage to all Traitless enemies, a good bonus considering the rarity of such units. His Long Distance ability allows him to hit enemies beyond his standing range, which is also useful as he stands only at 340. When protected properly, even Deadly Stages such as [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]] and [[Ogre Island (Deadly)|Ogre Island]] are easy to defeat, and all of the [[:Category:Crazed Cat Stages|Crazed Cat Stages]] become a joke if you have him. Notably, the only Crazed Cats that outrange him are [[Crazed Tank Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Tank Cat]], [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Lizard]] and [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird]] (which is better off countered by [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating units]]), but D'ark is often able to be Strengthened by them, usually ending in their defeat. This is slightly paralleled by their Manic counterparts (excluding Axe/Dark, as they can and will perma-freeze him).

He is also immune to [[Wave Attack]]s, letting him shut down essentially every [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave enemy]] in the game.

When strengthened, Valiant D'arktanyan's already high damage skyrockets, reaching about 112,200 damage per hit against Traitless enemies at Level 30. This makes almost all [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]] and other stages containing Traitless bosses a walk in the park, so long as D'ark outranges the boss in question. Valiant D'arktanyan's monstrous 48K strengthened DPS at level 50 against Traitless Enemies easily makes him one of the best anti-traitless Ubers, supported by his short cooldown and relatively low cost for his amazing utility. However, it is not recommended to use Valiant D'arktanyan against enemies that outrange him, as he can be easily knocked back. Thus, unless you are confident he is able to attack before getting knocked back, only use in stages where he will either outrange the enemies, or where there are many peons at the front for him to use as stepping stones for his Long Distance ability.

Despite him being anti-Traitless, he still has 10k strengthened DPS against traited enemies, which is among the highest in the game for LD attackers generally. This allows him to work well as a generalist, performing spectacularly even outside of Traitless Enemies. Notably, his DPS against traited enemies while strengthened is also quite close to [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Meow-sketeer]]'s. However, you do have to note that he does half the damage initially (Until the 2nd knockback). Therefore, the DPS is inconsistent, resulting in a lower average DPS.

